COMMON TRAPS

- ⚠️ Bulk P-type and N-type semiconductors are ELECTRICALLY NEUTRAL, not charged.
- ⚠️ Negative terminal voltage does not mean Reverse Bias; check ΔV = V_P - V_N (e.g., V_P = -2 V, V_N = -7 V → ΔV = +5 V > 0 → Forward Bias).
- ⚠️ Reverse saturation current I_S does NOT increase with applied reverse voltage; it is saturated and limited by thermal minority carrier generation rate (doubles every 10 °C).
- ⚠️ Depletion layer contains fixed space charge ions ONLY, zero mobile charge carriers.
- ⚠️ Diffusion current flows P → N (majority); Drift current flows N → P (minority).
- ⚠️ Depletion width is asymmetric: extends deeper into lighter-doped side (x_P / x_N = N_D / N_A).
- ⚠️ In real forward-biased diode circuits, subtract knee voltage V_k from supply voltage: V_net = V_supply - V_k.
- ⚠️ Carbon is an insulator, not a semiconductor, due to small atomic size and unbreakable covalent bonds at room temp.
- ⚠️ In Boolean algebra, A + A = A (not 2A) and A · A = A (not A²).

